### National Law (Health Practitioner Regulation National Law Act 2009) in South Australia

#### **Mandatory Notifications**
Registered health practitioners, employers, and education providers must report certain types of conduct to the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). These include:

- **Impairment**: When a practitioner has a physical or mental impairment that places the public at substantial risk of harm.
- **Intoxication**: When a practitioner is intoxicated by alcohol or drugs while practicing.
- **Significant Departure from Professional Standards**: When a practitioner's conduct significantly departs from accepted professional standards.
- **Sexual Misconduct**: Any sexual misconduct by a practitioner [1](https://www.ahpra.gov.au/Notifications/mandatorynotifications/Mandatory-notifications.aspx).

#### **Additional Reporting Requirements**
- **Reasonable Belief**: Before making a mandatory notification, a notifier must form a reasonable belief that the incident or behavior occurred and poses a risk to the public [1](https://www.ahpra.gov.au/Notifications/mandatorynotifications/Mandatory-notifications.aspx).
- **Different Thresholds**: There are different thresholds for making a mandatory notification depending on whether the notifier is a treating practitioner, non-treating practitioner, employer, or education provider [1](https://www.ahpra.gov.au/Notifications/mandatorynotifications/Mandatory-notifications.aspx).
- **Voluntary Notifications**: Anyone can make a voluntary notification (submit a concern) about a registered health practitioner or student [1](https://www.ahpra.gov.au/Notifications/mandatorynotifications/Mandatory-notifications.aspx).

These requirements ensure that health practitioners maintain high standards of professional conduct and that any risks to public safety are promptly addressed.

[1](https://www.ahpra.gov.au/Notifications/mandatorynotifications/Mandatory-notifications.aspx): [AHPRA - Mandatory Notifications](https://www.ahpra.gov.au/Notifications/mandatorynotifications/Mandatory-notifications.aspx)